# ADO role delivery checklist

When you create or materially change an `infra.ado` role under `roles/`, do **all** of the following in the same effort—not just the role itself.

## 1. Role quality

- Keep/update `roles/<role>/README.md` (purpose, requirements, variables, example playbook, tags)
- Add an antsibull-changelog fragment under `changelogs/fragments/`
- Run / fix `yamllint` and `ansible-lint` for touched role paths
- Register the component in `bootstrap_resolve_component/files/components_defaults.yml` when Contoller playbooks use `component:` + resolve

## 2. Bootstrap templates (collection)

Wire the role into Contoller scaffolding generators:

- Playbook template under `roles/bootstrap_generate_playbook_repo/files/playbooks/...`
- Job template seed under `roles/bootstrap_controller/files/job_templates/...`
- Use the shared OpenShift auth pattern: `vault_openshift.yml` + `vars_openshift.yml` and `K8S_AUTH_HOST`/`K8S_AUTH_API_KEY` from `host`/`token` (same as Grafana/Quay/OpenShift playbooks)

## 3. Preflight UI

Add the component as a selectable option in `ado-preflight-ui` (e.g. `openshiftApps` / `component_config` / labels) so generate/bootstrap can emit it.

## 4. Contoller project (lab)

When validating in the lab Contoller project (`bootstrap-sample` / `provision`), vendor or sync the role + playbook + JT so CLI and Contoller both work.
